  "title": "Engagement Under an NSE Exception",
  "setting": "At a CCMD, before a proposed engagement; the time and geographic location are not specified.",
  "decider": "The commander responsible for the engagement under established ROE",
  "agent_recast": false,
  "recast_note": "",
  "agent": "The commander responsible for the engagement under established ROE",
  "agent_role": "decide",
  "situation": "The commander is considering an engagement involving an NSE. The ordinary process requires removing the entity from the NSL and recording it on the JTL or RTL, as appropriate, before strikes. The decision point falls within one of the stated exception categories: intelligence confirms military use and the need is time-sensitive, or troops are taking hostile fire from NSEs. In those instances, the entity need not be reflected on the JTL before it can be engaged. Operational imperatives and established ROE provide authority to engage unless supplemental ROE expressly limits that authority, including the inherent right and obligation of self-defense.",
  "question": "What should the commander responsible for the engagement do when an NSE falls within a stated exception: authorize engagement under the exception or decline engagement pending ordinary status-change and JTL/RTL processing?",
  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "F1",
      "kind": "situation",
      "status": "confirmed",
      "fact": "Before strikes, the ordinary process requires removing the NSE from the NSL.",
      "spans": [
        "src:f14afcd731ae#p43.4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F2",
      "kind": "situation",
      "status": "confirmed",
      "fact": "The entity identification number must be placed with the appropriate secondary hostile CATCODE or function code on the JTL or RTL, as appropriate.",
      "spans": [
        "src:f14afcd731ae#p43.4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F3",
      "kind": "authority",
      "status": "confirmed",
      "fact": "Unless higher authority designates otherwise, the CCDR or a designated representative is the only command level authorized to change an entity's NSL status.",
      "spans": [
        "src:f14afcd731ae#p43.4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F4",
      "kind": "situation",
      "status": "confirmed",
      "fact": "Close and timely coordination among the CCMD, Joint Staff Targeting, and the appropriate RACs is imperative.",
      "spans": [
        "src:f14afcd731ae#p43.4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F5",
      "kind": "situation",
      "status": "confirmed",
      "fact": "Changes to the NSL must be documented by DTG and reason.",
      "spans": [
        "src:f14afcd731ae#p43.4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F6",
      "kind": "intelligence",
      "status": "confirmed",
      "fact": "One stated exception applies when intelligence confirms military use of the NSE and the need to strike is time-sensitive.",
      "spans": [
        "src:f14afcd731ae#p43.5",
        "src:f14afcd731ae#p43.6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F7",
      "kind": "situation",
      "status": "confirmed",
      "fact": "Another stated exception applies when troops are in contact and taking hostile fire from NSEs.",
      "spans": [
        "src:f14afcd731ae#p43.5",
        "src:f14afcd731ae#p43.7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F8",
      "kind": "authority",
      "status": "confirmed",
      "fact": "In the stated exceptions, the entity need not be reflected on the JTL before engagement.",
      "spans": [
        "src:f14afcd731ae#p43.8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F9",
      "kind": "authority",
      "status": "confirmed",
      "fact": "Unless SecDef-provided supplemental ROE expressly limits the authority, operational imperatives and established ROE provide authority to engage in these instances, including the inherent right and obligation of self-defense.",
